# Blur Circles — non-interactive Skia scene: a sweep-gradient circle and a
# frosted "glass" circle wander around the centre, each driven by simplex
# noise evaluated in a worklet off a 20 s ping-pong clock (withRepeat).
# What this test covers: letting the noise-driven animation run for a long
# stretch (worklet noise2D + clip rrect every frame), taps and sideways drags
# on the canvas (must be ignored), and a short pull-down that starts the app's
# close drag and is released early (card springs back while the canvas keeps
# animating), then more run time before closing.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/blur-circles"
wait 2000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 30000
wait 5000
press 201 437
wait 300
press 80 700
wait 300
gesture pan 100 600 200 0 500
wait 400
gesture pan 300 300 -200 -40 400
wait 2000
# Small pull-down: below the close threshold, the demo must stay open.
gesture pan 201 500 0 60 600
wait 1500
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
wait 6000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
